A JavaScript module isusually a file, but it can also bean HTML script.

A module fileis a .js file using import / export.

A module scriptis an HTML script using import / export.

Modules useexportandimportto interchange functionalities between modules.

An HTML script usingtype="module"is treated as a module:

### Code Snippets

```
// Export an "add" function
export function add(a, b) {
return a + b;
}

---

// Import an "add" function
import { add } from './math.js';
let result = add(2, 3);

---

// Export an "add" function
export function add(a, b) {
return a + b;
}

---

<script type="module">
// Import the add function
import { add } from './math.js';
let result = add(2, 3);
</script>

---

// Export name and age
export const name = "Jesse";
export const age = 40;

---

<script type="module">
// Import name and age
import { name, age } from "./person.js";
</script>

---

const message = () => {
const name = "Jesse";
const age = 40;
return name + ' is ' + age + 'years old.';
};
export default message;

---

<script type="module">
import message from "./message.js";
</script>
```
